  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p45.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The arithmetic-geometric mean inequality gives \\[ \\frac{a+b}{2}\\gt\\sqrt{ab} \\] for unequal positive \\(a,b.\\) Applying the same inequality to \\(\\frac{1}{a}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{b}\\) gives \\[ \\sqrt{ab}\\gt\\frac{2ab}{a+b}. \\] Therefore the decreasing order is arithmetic mean, geometric mean, harmonic mean.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Recognize the arithmetic, geometric, and harmonic means of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\)",
        "For unequal positive numbers, the mean inequalities are strict"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
